    {"day": 15, "title": "Project: Task Manager App", "time": "90 min", "lang": "javascript", "type": "project",
     "lesson": "# Project: Task Manager App\n\nTime to combine everything from Phase 3! Build a full Task Manager with React.\n\n## Requirements\n\n1. **Task CRUD**: Create, read, update, delete tasks\n2. **Categories**: Organize tasks by category (Work, Personal, Study)\n3. **Priorities**: High, Medium, Low with visual indicators\n4. **Filters**: Filter by category, priority, completion status\n5. **Persistence**: Save to localStorage\n6. **Responsive**: Works on mobile and desktop\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nApp\n├── Header (title + add button)\n├── FilterBar (category, priority, status filters)\n├── TaskList\n│   └── TaskItem (checkbox, title, category badge, delete)\n└── AddTaskModal (form with title, category, priority)\n```\n\n## Tips\n\n- Use `useState` for tasks array and filter state\n- Use `useEffect` to sync with localStorage\n- Extract reusable components (Badge, Modal, Select)\n- Keep state as high as needed, but no higher",
     "assignment": "Build the Task Manager:\n- Add task form with title, category, priority\n- Display tasks in a list with completion toggle\n- Filter tasks by category and priority\n- Delete tasks with confirmation\n- Persist to localStorage\n- Track completion statistics",
     "starter": "// Task Manager App\nimport { useState, useEffect } from 'react';\n\nfunction TaskManager() {\n  const [tasks, setTasks] = useState([]);\n  const [filter, setFilter] = useState({ category: 'all', priority: 'all' });\n  \n  // Load from localStorage on mount\n  useEffect(() => {\n    const saved = localStorage.getItem('tasks');\n    if (saved) setTasks(JSON.parse(saved));\n  }, []);\n  \n  // Save to localStorage on change\n  useEffect(() => {\n    localStorage.setItem('tasks', JSON.stringify(tasks));\n  }, [tasks]);\n  \n  // Implement CRUD operations\n  \n  return null; // Build your JSX\n}\n\nconsole.log('Build the Task Manager');"},
