    {"day": 27, "title": "Docker & Containerization", "time": "50 min", "lang": "html", "type": "code",
     "lesson": "# Docker & Containerization\n\n## Why Docker?\n\nDocker packages your app with all its dependencies into a container that runs anywhere.\n\n## Dockerfile\n\n```dockerfile\n# Python backend\nFROM python:3.11-slim\nWORKDIR /app\nCOPY requirements.txt .\nRUN pip install --no-cache-dir -r requirements.txt\nCOPY . .\nEXPOSE 8000\nCMD [\"uvicorn\", \"app.main:app\", \"--host\", \"0.0.0.0\", \"--port\", \"8000\"]\n```\n\n## Docker Compose\n\n```yaml\nversion: '3.8'\nservices:\n  backend:\n    build: ./backend\n    ports:\n      - '8000:8000'\n    environment:\n      - DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///./data/app.db\n    volumes:\n      - ./data:/app/data\n  \n  frontend:\n    build: ./frontend\n    ports:\n      - '3000:3000'\n    depends_on:\n      - backend\n```\n\n## Key Commands\n\n```bash\ndocker build -t myapp .          # Build image\ndocker run -p 8000:8000 myapp    # Run container\ndocker compose up -d             # Start all services\ndocker compose down              # Stop all\n```",
     "assignment": "Write Docker configuration for a full-stack app:\n1. Dockerfile for the Python backend\n2. Dockerfile for the Next.js frontend\n3. docker-compose.yml that runs both services\n4. Add health checks to both services\n5. Use multi-stage builds for smaller images",
     "starter": "# Write your Dockerfiles and docker-compose.yml\n# Use comments to explain each line\n\n# --- Backend Dockerfile ---\n# FROM python:3.11-slim\n# ...\n\n# --- Frontend Dockerfile ---\n# FROM node:20-alpine\n# ...\n\n# --- docker-compose.yml ---\n# version: '3.8'\n# services:\n# ...\n\nconsole.log('Write your Docker config!');"},
